WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.090
Napoleon Dynamite is the kind of movie that
rewards repeat viewings, thanks to some very

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.460
subtle jokes and hints.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.680
There are plenty of odd details you just can't
catch the first time around because you're

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.680
too distracted by all of the other odd details.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.000
Here are a few.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.160
When we first meet Kip, it doesn't seem like
he's particularly honest about how he spends

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:20.660
his time:

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.280
"Napoleon, don't be jealous that I've been
chatting online with babes all day."

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.180
In fact, Kip notes that it's one babe in particular
who he spends hours talking to.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.280
Late in the film, we finally meet Kip's lady
love, LaFawnduh, who arrives on a bus and

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.080
quickly becomes an inseparable part of Kip's
life.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.360
Kip and LaFawnduh are clearly different in
just about every way, but they're able to

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.720
start a relationship surprisingly well.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.190
It's actually quite touching on some level,
but since Kip was also bragging to Napoleon

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.320
about another lie:

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.960
"Besides, we both know that I'm training to
become a cage fighter."

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:54.960
"Since when, Kip?

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.980
You have the worst reflexes of all time."

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.360
"Try and hit me Napoleon."

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:03.389
We're left to wonder: what exactly did Kip
tell LaFawnduh about himself to get her interested

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:04.380
in the first place?

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.640
From the moment we first see Uncle Rico, it
becomes clear that he's an unusual man.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.480
He spends a lot of his downtime throwing footballs
and recording himself doing quarterback moves

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.320
on his camcorder.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:20.920
Rico is a man pining for the glory days when
he was a high school star with prospects,

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.780
but it turns out his particular delusions
of grandeur sometimes reach dangerous heights.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.940
"How much you wanna make a bet I can throw
a football over them mountains?

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.220
Yeah."

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.670
Uncle Rico is desperate enough to believe
that he can purchase a device that will allow

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.320
him to travel through time.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:45.140
It's alarming that this delusional man has
been placed in charge of two young relatives,

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.780
one of whom is still in high school.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:51.579
He might have the best intentions, and he
might have some profound sadness in his life,

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:54.900
but Uncle Rico is frighteningly out of touch
with reality.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.680
Speaking of that time machine, we get to see
it in action when Napoleon discovers it laying

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.760
out on the dining room table and opts to give
it a try.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.600
After reading the instructions, Napoleon has
Kip plug the device in.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.100
He's immediately and violently electrocuted
until his brother pulls the plug.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.060
What makes the scene a little disturbing actually
comes at the moment when Kip lets a smile

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.700
cross his face as Napoleon writhes in pain.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.370
Siblings will fight, and we've all been guilty
of laughing just a little too much when a

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:28.820
friend or relative was injured in some minor
way, but Kip's smile here feels slightly creepy.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.660
Did he know the time machine wouldn't really
hurt Napoleon that much?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.260
Did he just not care?

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.360
Is he slightly sociopathic?

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.660
We'll never know.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.620
Pedro is a character who stands out in the
landscape of Napoleon's high school.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.860
This is part of what draws Napoleon to him,
but it also creates a strange relationship

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.080
between Pedro and other adults and students
at the school.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.180
It reaches its apex late in the film, when
Summer is giving her student body president

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:55.680
speech:

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.460
"Who wants to eat chiminy-changas next year?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.160
Not me.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.900
See, with me, it'll be summer all year long."

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:08.340
It's an obvious reference to Pedro's Mexican
heritage, and it's part of a pattern of casual

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.100
racism that lingers at various points in the
film.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.300
Be nicer to Pedro, people!

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:18.080
The film's most famous scene occurs during
the student body president assembly.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:23.500
Pedro, in need of a skit to support his candidacy,
is ready to give up, but then Napoleon shows

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.420
off his sweet dance moves to the tune of Jamiroquai's
"Canned Heat."

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.920
It's a classic moment of 2000s cinema, and
it's largely thanks to LaFawnduh, who, upon

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.689
learning Napoleon is interested in dance,
tosses him an unmarked cassette and tells

00:03:37.689 --> 00:03:38.780
him that her cousin made it.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.620
Now, that could just be a mix tape that her
cousin made, but we're given no label to tell

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:44.120
us that.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.680
So, keeping in mind that this is a stretch…
is LaFawnduh's cousin Jamiroquai?

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.660
Uncle Rico is a man with a many flaws.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:57.620
He's constantly looking to the past, he's
a bully to Napoleon, he enlists Kip as a pawn

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.980
in his schemes, and he also happens to be
a bit of an egotistical liar.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.100
As the film goes on, though, his sleazier
side sometimes takes a turn toward the full-blown

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:07.600
creepy.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.540
Yes, his delusions often make him into a buffoon,
but consider various incidents in the film

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.420
that escalate nearer to the end.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.900
He tries to get Trisha and Summer to try his
breast enhancement scheme, then corners Deb

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:24.540
at her photo studio, tells her to call him
"Uncle Rico," and passes her a brochure while

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.820
lying that it was Napoleon's idea.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.100
Then, of course, there's the moment with Rex's
wife Starla.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.900
"I don't feel comfortable reading this."

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.100
"Oh, that's fine, that's fine.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.940
But do you feel comfortable with me?"

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:43.360
Finally, the post-credits scene puts the icing
on the creepy cake when he sniffs LaFawnduh's

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.040
garter after catching it at the wedding.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.440
It's played for laughs, but it's also pretty
unnerving.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.040
Early in the film, Napoleon helps to establish
his particular brand of awkwardness by telling

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:59.410
Pedro that he doesn't have "any skills," lamenting
that he's not a martial arts master or computer

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.860
hacker, though he is able to draw a little.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.740
But as the story unfolds, Napoleon just keeps
proving himself wrong.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:11.140
At the FFA competition, he's able analyze
milk correctly with almost no hesitation.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:15.540
He's able to learn the dance that wins the
election for Pedro in a matter of days simply

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.940
by practicing diligently.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.600
Then, he reveals his fishing skills.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.140
"I caught you a delicious bass."

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:26.660
And in the post-credits scene, he's tamed
the horse Kip and LaFawnduh are supposed to

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.660
ride away on.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:32.380
It's a heartwarming ending; the film proves
that Napoleon does indeed have skills.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.380
He just has to go on a journey to realize
what they are.

